From d78880bcc49295b56ac4eea4031f1ab226a0cdc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:28:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(front): decline a replaced operator only where what TLC
 evaluates reaches it

TLC evaluates a definition with parameters only where something it
evaluates applies it, so a wrapper of TransitiveClosure's Warshall
that nothing applies never runs the Java method TLC replaces it with.
The front end declined any spec whose text named the replaced
operator, even in such a wrapper. It now follows the names from what
TLC may evaluate: every definition without parameters, every
assumption, every INSTANCE's substitutions and every name the
configuration gives, through the definitions and the LET definitions
those name, and declines only where that reaches the replaced
operator. An unused `<-` substitute and an unused definition without
parameters still count, since TLC may compute them. No run of the
upstream conformance suite changes; 39 of 90 generated specs around
such wrappers that declined now match TLC.
